 "read_me_first": "Every record in the ledger is in exactly one bucket of the closed set, and every mechanism is listed even at zero — the failure this step exists to fix was 17,614 due records sitting in no bucket at all while an hourly roll-up reported the number and nothing acted on it. `graded` is read back OFF the ledger after the resolver ran, never predicted. `NO_BAR_FOR_RESOLUTION_DATE` is not a fault in the record: the local panel ends at `bars.last_bar` and those records grade on a later day. Nothing here computes a return: `belief_state.resolve_one` does, with every guard it already had.",
